# Decompiled Refined Storage, Cable Tiers and Step Crafter sources.
#
# NOT IGNORED BECAUSE IT IS BIG -- 20 MB is nothing. Ignored because it is somebody
# else's source code, recovered from their jars for reference. Committing it to a public
# repository would redistribute Refined Storage's code under our name, which is both a
# licensing problem and a discourteous thing to do to a project we depend on and hope to
# stay on good terms with. Regenerate it locally instead; see SETUP.md.
decompiled/

# Dev-run leftovers. These are the ones that would quietly turn a 0.5 MB repository into a
# 6 GB one, so they are listed explicitly rather than trusted to a pattern:
#   worlds/    5.3 GB  the survival-rsperf test world
#   *.hprof    864 MB  a JVM heap dump -- also a raw image of everything in memory at the
#                      time, so it is not something to publish even if it were small
worlds/
saves/
logs/
libs/
*.hprof
*.log

# Scratch files from earlier sessions, kept locally, not part of the project
cp.txt
cp-out.txt
build-log.txt
scratchpad/
